L1 sigmoid soft-step detectors: new, cnp, risky, big, velo, small, night, far. L2 ReLU AND units: A3=relu(sum['new', 'cnp', 'risky', 'big']-2) w=1.5; A4=relu(sum['new', 'cnp', 'risky', 'big']-3) w=5.5; B3=relu(sum['velo', 'small', 'cnp']-2) w=8.4; C3=relu(sum['night', 'far', 'cnp']-2) w=8.4. Output bias -5.4=log-odds of residual fraud rate (~0.45%) outside the three signatures (new account+CNP+risky merchant+big amount; card-testing burst: >=7 txns/24h + tiny amount + CNP; night + >250km from home + CNP). Weights = log-odds of each signature cell rate (~95%, shrunk) minus base.
